Echo On

// Numeric constants
Assert ０ｘ０ === 0x0
Assert ＋０ｘ０ === +0x0
Assert ０ｘＦＦ＿ＦＦ＿ＦＦ === 0xff_ff_ff
Assert －０ｘ８０００＿００００ === -0x8000_0000
Assert ０ｏ０ === 0O0
Assert ０ｏ７７７＿７７７ === 0o777_777
Assert －０ｏ４００ === -0o400
Assert ０ｂ０ === 0B0
Assert ０ｂ１１１１＿００００ === 0B1111_0000
Assert －０ｂ１０００ === -0b1000
Assert ０ === Zero
Assert －０ === -0
Assert ＋０ === +0
Assert １２３ === 123
Assert －１２３ === -123
Assert ０．０ === 0.0
Assert －０．０ === -0.0
Assert １．２３ｅ４ === 1.23E4
Assert １．２３ｅ＋４ === 1.23E+4
Assert ＋１．２３ｅ＋４ === 1.23E+4
Assert －１．２３ｅ－４ === -1.23E-4

// Operators
// NB: Spaces around operators generally recommended
//     and required for +/- when preceeding a
//     numeric constant
// TODO: fix op precedence so we don't need the parens!
Assert (5 ＋ 3) === (5 + 3)
Assert (5 － 3) === (5 - 3)
Assert (5 ＊ 3) === (5 * 3)
Assert (5 ／ 3) === (5 / 3)
Assert (5 ％ 3) === (5 % 3)
Assert (5 ＆ 3) === (5 & 3)
Assert (5 ｜ 3) === (5 | 3)
Assert (5 ＾ 3) === (5 ^ 3)
Assert (5 ＊＊ 3) === (5 ** 3)
Assert (5 ＜＜ 3) === (5 << 3)
Assert (5 ＞＞ 3) === (5 >> 3)

Assert (True ＆＆ False) === (True && False)
Assert (True ＆＆ True) === (True && True)

Assert (False ｜｜ True) === (False || True)
Assert (False ｜｜ False) === (False || False)

Assert "abc"［1］ === "abc"[1]
Assert "abc"［1：2］ === "abc"[1:2]

Set a＝5；// fullwidth = and ;
Assert a == 5.0
Assert a ＝＝ 5.0 // fullwidth =
Assert a === 5
Assert a ＝＝＝ 5 // fullwidth =

// NB: fullwidth parens not yet supported
Function f(x，y) -> x＋y // fullwidth command and plus
Assert ＠f(5，3) === @f(5,3) // fullwidth at and comma

Echo Off
